{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1548630-looking-for-players-werewolf-the-apocalypse-on-discord-or-irl","id":1548630,"title":"Looking for players Werewolf the Apocalypse on Discord or IRL.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-20T13:02:50-08:00","id":1548630,"title":"Looking for players Werewolf the Apocalypse on Discord or IRL.","content":"Hello. I am looking for players to run a Werewolf the Apocalypse game. Preferably IRL (I am located about an hour and a half north of Chicago, and about an hour south of Kenosha). I been running and playing WOD (mostly Werewolf the Apocalypse), for the last 20 years. I started at the very beginning of 2nd edition. Few things that I promise you in my game<br /> a) POLITICS. This aspect is often ignored by Werewolf the Apocalypse Storytellers. Wolves are SOCIAL creatures, so in Garou society there are lots of politics and interactions going on. Not just between different tribes, but also between different camps within one tribe. For example, Wise Guys have very little in common with Cyber Dogs, and most likely are not best buddies with City Farmers and Urban Primitives. Wolves, by their nature, seek dominance and power. There is a LOT of politics SHOULD be going on, but it is ignored. Werewolf has every chance to be as political as Vampire.<br /> b) Mysticism. Mysteries of umbra, spirit world, rituals, ritual magic, ancient relics and history, travel between the worlds. All that is also open for exploration.<br /> c) Investigation. When something goes very bad. It is not always &quot;Pentex&quot; or &quot;Fomori&quot; or &quot;Wyrm&quot;, it is often something else entirely. Remember, Adolf Hitler was a human, and NOT a Fomori. &quot;Darkness lives in hearts of men&quot;. So it is NOT always Wyrm, or Pentex.<br /> d) &quot;Nothing is what it seems, not even me&quot;. Another aspect of the World of Darkness is ignored. Who is a True Enemy? Wyrm? Or maybe someone who has done MUCH more damage to Gaia and Tellurian then Wyrm itself. Who can it be?<br /> <br /> Please, let me know if interested. Of course, I will do my best to tailor my story to what YOU, my players and YOUR CHARACTERS, want.<br /> Looking forward to hearing from you all.<br /> <br /> P.S. I am playing on rules mostly from W20 with 2e rules thrown in. Any gift, any merit and flaw, from ANY edition are allowed with my approval. It is about STORY, not about &quot;gifts&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26712-tigerclaw_x","name":"Tigerclaw_x","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}